{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00952",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 11.49,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "Dr Hughes, this is Arlo, he's five, and his mum is here about his snoring. I'll leave you to it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.58,
      "end_seconds": 21.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Thanks, nurse. Hello Arlo, hello Mum. What's been going on? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 24.55,
      "end_seconds": 32.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "He snores. Properly, like a lorry. It's been about a year, getting worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.48,
      "end_seconds": 37.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I don't snore. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 40.81,
      "end_seconds": 47.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "You do, sweetheart. I recorded it, I've got it on my phone. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.9,
      "end_seconds": 55.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Could I hear a bit of it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 58.58,
      "end_seconds": 61.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Of course. Here you go. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.27,
      "end_seconds": 70.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Goodness. That's loud. Does he stop breathing at all, in the night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 73.67,
      "end_seconds": 80.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Sometimes it sounds like he pauses. Not for long. A few seconds."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.42,
      "end_seconds": 88.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Does he have a fever at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 90.36,
      "end_seconds": 92.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "No fever, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.63,
      "end_seconds": 96.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Any trouble swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 99.76,
      "end_seconds": 103.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "None, he eats like a horse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.11,
      "end_seconds": 109.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "And during the day, how's he? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 112.38,
      "end_seconds": 121.55,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "A bit cranky by the afternoon. He used to nap, and he doesn't now. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.22,
      "end_seconds": 128.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "And does he ever wake up grumpy or tired? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 131.31,
      "end_seconds": 135.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Yes, he's often grumpy first thing. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.17,
      "end_seconds": 143.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Is there a history of tonsil problems, Mum?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 146.3,
      "end_seconds": 149.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "He's had tonsillitis twice, last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.81,
      "end_seconds": 155.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Where's he at in school?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 157.57,
      "end_seconds": 160.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Reception, at the village primary."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.29,
      "end_seconds": 169.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Arlo, can you open your mouth wide like a lion? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.78,
      "end_seconds": 173.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Roar! ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.02,
      "end_seconds": 179.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Perfect. Can you do it again? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.52,
      "end_seconds": 184.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Roar! ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.94,
      "end_seconds": 201.43,
      "duration_seconds": 14.49,
      "text": "Thank you, I can see. Mum, I'm going to explain what I'm looking for. Tonsils sit at the back of the throat. In some children, they are very big. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 204.65,
      "end_seconds": 207.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Are his big? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.92,
      "end_seconds": 220.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.38,
      "text": "I'll tell you after I've explained what the options are. Sometimes big tonsils can narrow the airway at night. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 222.15,
      "end_seconds": 226.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Is that what's causing the snoring? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.88,
      "end_seconds": 245.03,
      "duration_seconds": 17.15,
      "text": "It might be. I won't put a label on it today. I'd like to arrange an overnight oxygen level test at home, so we can see how he breathes while he sleeps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 248.1,
      "end_seconds": 251.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "How does that work? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.07,
      "end_seconds": 264.75,
      "duration_seconds": 10.68,
      "text": "A small sensor goes on his toe, and it records through the night. The nurse will give you the kit. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 266.05,
      "end_seconds": 271.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "I'll get it ready for you, Mrs Webb. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 273.97,
      "end_seconds": 276.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "And then? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.17,
      "end_seconds": 287.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "Then we'll know whether it's a simple snore or whether it affects his sleep. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 289.67,
      "end_seconds": 293.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "That makes sense. Thank you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.13,
      "end_seconds": 301.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Arlo, you were a very good lion. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.13,
      "end_seconds": 306.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Rrrr! ~"
    }
  ]
}
